{
  "_about": [
    "THE COLLECTIONS THE READ PATH NEEDS (TASK-L169 §1). The source of truth for this template's schema: NodeGX keeps a collection's schema in the backend, not the project, so tools/setup-backend.mjs applies this file through POST /admin/schema/apply.",
    "One collection per PRODUCT TABLE a page reads, named after it (PascalCase singular). Only the columns a payload reads. No `id` column: it is reserved at the adapter layer (FED-002 R3/R14), so the product's key is a named field with a unique index.",
    "Domain timestamps (completedAt, startsAt, dueAt, …) are ISO-8601 STRINGS, not Date: a read function serialises them exactly as the product's JSON does. createdAt/updatedAt are the backend's own and are carried over from the product by admin import.",
    "NOT ENFORCED HERE, and the read path does not need them: enum values are plain strings (sprint 50's write functions validate them); the product's CHECK constraints coaching_sessions_one_scope, assignments_one_scope and session_prep_one_target have no NodeGX equivalent (index declarations take fields/unique/order only); and learning_path_steps' unique (path_id, position) holds only on LIVE rows in the product (L113) — declared here only because the seed carries no removed step. A partial unique index is part of OpenNoodl HLT-016.",
    "LearnerProfile.userId and ConversationMessage.authorUserId are a _User's objectId. seed.json names users by username (it cannot know an objectId), and tools/setup-backend.mjs resolves them when it creates the users — the product's learner_profiles.account_id, one layer over."
  ],
